GPU keep-warm (0215) within the compatibility-mode limits. Its compute shader used
@workgroup_size(256), above the 128 that a device without core features and limits allows (Linux on
OpenGL ES, e.g. llvmpipe or a GPU without Vulkan): the first time keep-warm engaged, the pipeline
creation was a fatal uncaptured validation error. Now 128 invocations per workgroup and 32768
workgroups (the same 4 Mi invocations; at most 65535 workgroups per dimension in compatibility mode),
and the shader and pipeline are created inside an error scope, so a failure turns keep-warm off.

diff --git a/lib/aurora.cpp b/lib/aurora.cpp
